บ                     3.0     Platform Integration                           บ
บ                                                                            บ
บ   How can the selected UNIX platform(s) be integrated with existing        บ
บ   Mainframe, Midrange and PC technical architectures and applications ?    บ
ศออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออผ

        In general the selected UNIX platforms will need to be able to 
        communicate with all the existing Mainframe, Midrange and PC's 
        currently operating.  The method of communication and the 
        information/access available will vary depending upon the system
        being interfaced.

        Mainframes :   
                Typically there will be some sort of file 
                access/transfer facilities between the mainframe and the
                selected UNIX platforms.

                There might also be some sort of terminal emulation running
                on the UNIX platforms in order to run applications on
                the mainframe from the UNIX platforms.

        Midrange :
                The interface between midrange systems and the UNIX platforms 
                would probably be similar to mainframe access, but with a 
                greater possibility for data sharing between applications on
                the two different systems.

        PC's :
                There are several ways of connecting PC's to the selected
                UNIX platforms these are discussed in the answer to question 
                6.0.

