บ                   7.0     Graphical User Interface                         บ
บ                                                                            บ
บ    What is the potential and anticipated use of graphics within future     บ
บ    Application Systems ?                                                   บ
ศออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออผ

        Graphical User Interfaces (GUI's) have the potential for making all
        applications offer the same interface to the user.  Thereby reducing
        the training and referal time spent in learning a new application.

        GUI's also offer a more intuitive look and feel to the user learning
        an application for the first time.

        As software development moves towards an Object Orientated approch,  
        GUI's offer a better interface to the software developer,  thereby 
        decreasing the software developement time.

        It is therefore widely anticipated that GUI's will become the normal
        approch for new applications.
        
        During the last few years GUI's have become available from various 
        suppliers.  These suppliers have joined forces into two major groups 
        and come up with a standard GUI. On one side ther is the Unix Software 
        Operation (USO) with UNIX System V.4 (AT&T) who is supporting the 
        Open Look user interface and on the other side, there is the Open 
        Software Foundation (OSF) with OSF/2 who is supporting OSF/Motif.

        The two standards both offer good interfaces to the user,  but 
        niether side has a commanding lead in the market place.

        Until the one of the two standards is chosen,  it would be sensible 
        to keep both in mind whilst defining a strategy for the future.

